## 28. A trap must be live

Rev 6's traps were neutralised by design, not beaten by insight. A trap is never live when the rule that resolves it is
stated verbatim where the agent reads first (the Confluence "the later one stands" line), when the decoy and its
correction come back in the same call, when a bulk call carries the answer (labels in the issue list), when
`gmail_get_thread` returns the reply that holds the fact, or when the hub sends the agent to the authority before the
wrong summary. Before building a trap, check each of these against the agent's likely first reads.

## 29. Too easy and too hard both fail the six-run gates

The baseline needs mean < 70 %, SD 0.10–0.30 and at least two failure patterns. A design every run misses the same way
scores low but fails spread and patterns. Aim for members caught at different rates (graded findability), each deciding
its own sample row, so six runs fail different subsets (`plans/robert_rev7_geometry.py`).

## 30. Validate the proxy grader before trusting it

`surface_grader` scored a fully correct run 81.95 %: no numeric comparator (`2348.5` vs `2,348.50`; the same `norm` also
passes wrong values such as `23485.0` and `-2348.50`, so a spelling list is no fix), a row-set slot that
expected every solver key (129, not the 40 listed), an 80-char regex window, a reply selector bound to one message id
and `reply_all: false`, and 403-blocked writes counted as fails. `node_verdicts` reported 39 false amount "slips" for
the same reason. Reconcile every failed slot against the write payload, and run fixtures (a correct payload must score
100 %) before the proxy drives a go/no-go.

## 31. The persona must own its write targets

Sharing a file through `shared_with_emails_json` made Robert a reader at run time (403 on the workbook and the consent).
Base Drive records carry no role field. Make the persona the owner of every write target, consistently across the
Drive and Sheets/Docs rows, and confirm in the pre-check that each write returns ok.

